,"html_url":"https://github.com/mooflu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mooflu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-23T18:39:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T18:39:35Z","body":"Looks like the \"double clicking on blank area\" was fixed here https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112941\n\nI can still trigger the error by double clicking (left or right mouse button) on an item in the scene tree dock when no node is selected.\nFor 4.6.rc2 the error is:\n`ERROR: editor/docks/scene_tree_dock.cpp:4202 - Parameter \"node\" is null.`\n\nI.e. `item_icon_double_clicked` is triggered here (tree.cpp): \n```\n\t\t\t\t} else if (mb->is_double_click() && get_item_at_position(mb->get_position()) != nullptr) {\n\t\t\t\t\temit_signal(SNAME(\"item_icon_double_clicked\"));\n\t\t\t\t}\n```\nand signal handler in scene_tree_dock.cpp \n```\n\tscene_tree->get_scene_tree()->connect(\"item_icon_double_clicked\", callable_mp(this, &SceneTreeDock::_focus_node));\n```\nhas the ERR_FAIL_NULL:\n```\n4200 void SceneTreeDock::_focus_node() {\n4201 \tNode *node = scene_tree->get_selected();\n4202 \tERR_FAIL_NULL(node);\n```\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3791733754/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_gi